          "fact_id": "VAL-001-002-F05",
          "status": "covered",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        }
      ],
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Before sending a DMCA takedown notice, a copyright owner should conduct an initial investigation to confirm both that they own the copyright to an original work and that the content on GitHub is unauthorized and infringing.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The investigation should include confirming that the use is not protected as fair use.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Just because a piece of code has a copyright notice does not necessarily mean it is infringing; it is possible the code is being used in accordance with an open-source license.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "You should review licenses and agreements to confirm the code is not authorized under any of them.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Before sending a takedown request, you must consider legal uses such as fair use and licensed uses.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A particular use may be fair if it only uses a small amount of copyrighted content, uses that content in a transformative way, uses it for educational purposes, or some combination of these.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Because code naturally lends itself to such uses, each use case is different and must be considered separately.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Identifying valid copyright infringement in code is more complicated than for photos, music, or videos.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A repository may contain bits of code from many people with only one file or sub-routine infringing.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Code mixes functionality with creative expression but copyright only protects expressive elements, not functional parts.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "There are often licenses to consider.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Code may be alleged to infringe in many different ways requiring detailed explanations.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "You can only use the DMCA process to target content protected by copyright.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Facts (including data), words and short phrases, and URLs and domain names are generally not copyrightable.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub can only accept DMCA notices for works protected by copyright that identify a specific copyrightable work.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub asks that you conduct a thorough investigation and consult with an attorney before submitting a takedown to make sure the use isn't actually permissible.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Speaking to a legal professional is doubly important when dealing with code.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If you have questions about whether your content is protectable, you should speak with a lawyer.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A great first step before sending a takedown notice is to try contacting the user directly via their public profile, the repository's README, or by opening an issue or pull request.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Contacting the user directly is not strictly required but is encouraged.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "DMCA notices must identify copyrighted work(s) allegedly being infringed; the process cannot be used for other complaints such as trademark infringement or sensitive data, which have separate processes.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The DMCA requires you to swear to the facts under penalty of perjury, and intentionally lying is a federal crime; submitting false information could also result in civil liability.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The DMCA provides for damages against anyone who knowingly materially misrepresents that material is infringing.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "There may be legal consequences for sending a false or frivolous takedown notice.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Your complaint will be published (after redaction of personal information) at GitHub's public DMCA repository.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The affected user may submit a counter notice, and if they do, GitHub will re-enable the content within 10–14 days unless you notify GitHub that you have initiated legal action seeking a court order to restrain the user.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If you wish to keep content disabled after a counter notice, you will need to initiate legal action, meaning you might get sued.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If you allege less than a whole repository infringes, you should identify the specific file(s) or line numbers.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub will not automatically disable forks when disabling a parent repository.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

