          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "It is possible that the code is being used in accordance with an open-source license.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A company should review licenses and agreements to confirm that the code on GitHub is not authorized under any of them before sending a takedown.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Before sending a takedown request, you must consider legal uses such as fair use and licensed uses.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A use may be fair if it uses only a small amount of copyrighted content, uses it transformatively, uses it for educational purposes, or some combination.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Because code naturally lends itself to such uses, each use case is different and must be considered separately.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Identifying valid copyright infringement in code is more complicated than for photos, music, or videos.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A repository may mix code from many people with only one file or sub-routine infringing.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Copyright protects expressive elements but not functional parts.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Licenses may apply.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Code may be alleged to infringe in many ways requiring detailed explanations.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Facts (including data), words and short phrases, and URLs/domain names are generally not copyrightable.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "You can only use the DMCA process to target content protected by copyright.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub only accepts DMCA notices for works protected by copyright that identify a specific copyrightable work.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub asks that you conduct a thorough investigation and consult with an attorney before submitting a takedown to make sure that the use isn't actually permissible.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Speaking to a legal professional is doubly important when dealing with code.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A great first step is to try contacting the user directly—via their public profile, the repository README, or by opening an issue or pull request.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Contacting the user first is not strictly required but is encouraged.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "You must swear to the facts under penalty of perjury, and intentionally lying is a federal crime.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Submitting false information could also result in civil liability.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The DMCA provides for damages against anyone who knowingly materially misrepresents that material is infringing.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "There may be legal consequences for sending a false or frivolous takedown notice.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub exercises little discretion beyond checking that notices meet minimum DMCA requirements; the parties and their lawyers evaluate the merits.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Affected users may submit a counter notice, and if they do, GitHub will re-enable the content within 10–14 days unless you notify GitHub that you have initiated legal action to restrain the user.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Your complaint will be published (after redaction of personal information) at GitHub's public DMCA repository.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The DMCA process is only for copyright infringement complaints; it cannot be used for trademark or sensitive-data complaints, which have separate processes.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If your concern is trademark abuse, sensitive data, or defamation/abusive behavior, different policies apply.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The provided policies do not specify a step-by-step pre-filing checklist beyond the above, nor do they describe how to compare code for copying (e.g., specific forensic or diff techniques).",
