          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A DMCA counter notice must provide contact information including email address, name, telephone number, and physical address.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A DMCA counter notice must include the submitter's physical or electronic signature.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A DMCA counter notice must include a sworn statement under penalty of perjury of a good-faith belief that the material was removed or disabled as a result of a mistake or misidentification.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A DMCA counter notice must include a statement consenting to the jurisdiction of the Federal District Court for the judicial district in which the submitter's address is located (or the Northern District of California if outside the United States) and accepting service of process from the person who provided the DMCA notification or their agent.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub asks the submitter to include the statement 'I have read and understand GitHub's Guide to Filing a DMCA Counter Notice,' but will not refuse to process an otherwise complete notice if that statement is missing.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The submitter swears to the counter notice under penalty of perjury; intentionally lying in a sworn declaration is a federal crime and could also result in civil liability.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The submitter must have a good-faith belief that the material was removed or disabled as a result of mistake or misidentification.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The submitter consents to jurisdiction and to accept service of process from the complaining party or their agent.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The submitter may get sued: if the complaining party wants to keep the content disabled, they must initiate a legal action seeking a court order, and the submitter consents to that in the counter notice.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub will wait 10–14 days and then re-enable the content unless the copyright owner initiates legal action before then.",
