          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The complaint must provide the complainant's contact information: email address, name, telephone number, and physical address.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The complaint should provide contact information for the alleged infringer, if known, usually satisfied by providing the GitHub username.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The complaint must include the good faith statement: \"I have a good faith belief that use of the copyrighted materials described above on the infringing web pages is not authorized by the copyright owner, or its agent, or the law. I have taken fair use into consideration.\"",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The complaint must include the perjury statement: \"I swear, under penalty of perjury, that the information in this notification is accurate and that I am the copyright owner, or am authorized to act on behalf of the owner, of an exclusive right that is allegedly infringed.\"",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The complaint must include the complainant's physical or electronic signature.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Because GitHub cannot disable access to specific files within a repository, if the notice does not allege that the entire repository or package infringes, GitHub will contact the repository creator and give them approximately 1 business day to delete or modify the content specified in the notice.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The user must notify GitHub within the approximately 1 business day window that they made the changes; if they do not, GitHub will disable the repository.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If the user notifies GitHub of changes, GitHub verifies the changes and notifies the copyright owner.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The copyright owner must review the changes and renew or revise the takedown notice if the changes are insufficient; GitHub will not take further action unless the owner contacts it to renew or revise.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If the owner is satisfied, they may submit a formal retraction or do nothing; silence longer than two weeks is interpreted as an implied retraction.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If the notice alleges that the entire contents of a repository infringe, or a package infringes, GitHub will skip the change opportunity and disable the entire repository or package expeditiously.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Because packages are immutable, if only part of a package is infringing, GitHub would need to disable the entire package, but permits reinstatement once the infringing portion is removed.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If the complaint involves circumvention of technical measures, additional detailed statements are required describing what the technical measures are, how they effectively control access to the copyrighted material, and how the accused project is designed to circumvent them.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

