          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Cookies allow GitHub to store and honor your preferences and settings, enable you to sign in, combat fraud, and analyze how its websites and online services are performing.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "A cookie can later be read when your browser connects to a web server in the same domain that placed it, allowing the server to recognize your browser over time.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Web beacons are electronic images (also called single-pixel or clear GIFs) contained within a website or email.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "When your browser opens a page or email containing a web beacon, it automatically connects to the web server hosting the image (typically a third party), which can log information about your device and set and read its own cookies.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub uses web beacons to help deliver cookies and gather usage and performance data, and its websites may include web beacons, cookies, or similar technologies from third-party service providers.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub uses cookies and similar technologies for purposes including storing preferences and settings, enabling sign-in, analyzing performance, tracking interactions, developing inferences, and combating fraud.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Some cookies and similar technologies may be provided by third parties, including service providers and advertising partners.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "You have a variety of tools to control data collected by cookies, web beacons, and similar technologies.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "You can use controls in your internet browser to limit how websites use cookies and to withdraw consent by clearing or blocking cookies.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "If your browser sends a Do Not Track (DNT) signal, GitHub will not set non-essential cookies and will not load third-party resources that set non-essential cookies.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Many browsers provide cookie controls that may limit the types of cookies you encounter; you can check your browser's documentation.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Browser extensions designed to block tracking (such as Privacy Badger) may disable non-essential cookies set by a website or third parties.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "Extensions designed to block unwanted content (such as uBlock Origin) will disable non-essential cookies to the extent that content setting them is blocked.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "You may use the Global Privacy Control (GPC) to communicate your privacy preferences; if GitHub detects the GPC signal, it will not share your data (GitHub states it does not sell your data).",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "GitHub's advertising partners may participate in associations providing ways to opt out of ad targeting, such as NAI and DAA (United States), the Digital Advertising Alliance of Canada (Canada), and the European Digital Advertising Alliance (Europe).",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "These choices are specific to the browser you are using; if you access the Services from other devices or browsers, you must take these actions from those systems for your choices to apply.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
          "note": ""
        },
        {
          "text": "The candidate-specific notice describes cookies and web beacons and general browser-based controls, while the more detailed control options (DNT, GPC, extensions, advertising opt-outs) appear in GitHub's General Privacy Statement, which is not specific to candidates.",
          "support_status": "supported",
          "citation_status": "supported",
